98048939027", "personaname": "Andrei SX", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198048939027/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 22, "playtime_forever": 24658, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 6387, "last_played": 1733490506, "avatar": "35c755fe1e8666e5843d7fcc28434005a8305ef4"}, "language": "english", "review": "Arma 3 does not have time to teach you how to play it. It does not have time to help you find someone to play with. It lacks the common decency to provide a story, of any kind, at release.\n\nBohemia Interactive's sandbox military simulation series began life in 2001 as Operation Flashpoint: Cold War Crisis before the developer retconned its own title, renaming the series Arma. Updating the game for modern PC players was a tall order, and after four long years of development Arma 3 still isn't done.\n\nBohemia Interactive made the decision to release it anyway.\n\nArma 3 may be the most challenging, and the most rewarding, online shooter I have ever played. But it's missing key components — most damning of all a single-player campaign. As a result, it feels more like a huge demo than a finished product.", "timestamp_created": 1416085742, "timestamp_updated": 1416085742, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.521276593208312988", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1378969200", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "12957226", "author": {"steamid": "76561198127146403", "personaname": "Insane Payne", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198127146403/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 8, "playtime_forever": 85244, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1654, "last_played": 1740416558, "avatar": "cc130acc9824b021a853765085d7eff788b524cb"}, "lang